When dealing with marital problems, there are a few different paths you can take. Here are a few suggestions:

*   Seek counseling: Couples therapy is a great way to address conflicts and work on communication skills. Many therapists offer couples counseling in addition to individual sessions.
*   Take a break: If things are getting too heated, it may be a good idea to give yourself and your partner some space. This can be a time to reflect on your feelings and thoughts, and to consider what you want to work on in your relationship.
*   Practice self-care: Take care of yourself by exercising regularly, eating well, and getting enough sleep.&#x20;
*   Reach out to friends and family: Talking to people who care about you can help you feel heard and validated.
